digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56786-x
  rankdir="TB";
  "Imp_1" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Autoimmune diseases involve autoantibodies (S1) and B cells play a pivotal role (S2)."];
  "Imp_11" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: AAV is B-cell mediated (S9) with IgG and damage (S10)."];
  "Imp_14" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Severe manifestations cause damage/death (S15, S16)."];
  "Imp_15" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: IgG rises precede relapses (S17) but associations variable (S18)."];
  "Imp_17" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Therapies improved management (S19) but require immunosuppression (S22)."];
  "Imp_2" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Targeting B cells offers insights (S3) but mechanisms are often unknown (S4)."];
  "Imp_21" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Understanding crucial (S24) given risks (S5)."];
  "Imp_23" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: ANCA/Anti-MPO directly pathogenic (S25) shown in mice (S26)."];
  "Imp_24" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Complement pathway crucial mediator (S27) and avacopan improves disease (S28)."];
  "Imp_26" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Anti-PR3 results vary (S29) but ANCA affects neutrophils (S30)."];
  "Imp_27" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: ANCA increases neutrophil cytotoxicity (S31) and NETs release complement components (S32)."];
  "Imp_34" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Challenging to study B cells (S33) but biology holds info (S34)."];
  "Imp_35" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: MPO-reactive B cells exist (S36) and are IgM-positive (S37)."];
  "Imp_7" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: B cells/antibodies assumed crucial (S20) supported by evidence (S21)."];
  "Imp_Rule_Final" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: Targeting offers insights (S3) and results relevant (S40)."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This study proposes to characterize circulating IgM-positive MPO-reactive autoreactive B-cell responses and anti-MPO IgM antibodies in MPO-positive ANCA-associated vasculitis, testing whether their complement-activating function contributes to pathogenicity and may inform future targeted therapeutic strategies.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) The retained and repaired terminal conclusions jointly motivate the paper-level research proposal."];
  "R21" [label="(0,0,0) Anti-MPO-ANCA are supported as directly pathogenic, and the alternative complement pathway has been identified as a crucial mediator specifically of anti-MPO-IgG-induced pathogenicity."];
  "R24" [label="(0,0,0) ANCA affect neutrophils by direct functional effects, increased endothelial adherence and cytotoxicity, and stimulation of NET release containing complement-activating components."];
  "R25" [label="(0,0,0) Prior ANCA and anti-MPO evidence links pathogenicity to neutrophil-mediated injury and complement-related mechanisms, without establishing from these premises alone that all ANCA-driven disease proceeds through complement activation."];
  "R30" [label="(0,0,0) Although specific B-cell responses underlying ANCA production have been challenging to study, circulating MPO-reactive B cells exist in AAV patients and most MPO-directed B cells are IgM-positive."];
  "R31" [label="(0,0,0) In the anti-MPO Ig response, anti-MPO IgM may have a prominent function, and the results highlight IgM B-cell autoreactivity as an important component of pathogenicity in this disease context."];
  "R43" [label="(0,0,0) The prominent function proposed for anti-MPO IgM may relate to complement activation, because this capacity is strongly dependent on anti-MPO IgM."];
  "S1" [label="(1,0,0) Many human autoimmune diseases are characterized by disease-specific autoantibodies."];
  "S10" [label="(10,0,0) AAV is hallmarked by the presence of disease-specific IgG and severe tissue damage."];
  "S15" [label="(15,0,0) The most severe AAV manifestations are alveolar hemorrhage and necrotizing crescentic glomerulonephritis (NCGN)."];
  "S16" [label="(16,0,0) These often cause irreversible organ damage and can be life-threatening."];
  "S17" [label="(17,0,0) The rise of ANCA-IgG often precedes relapses."];
  "S18" [label="(18,0,0) Associations between ANCA-IgG levels and disease activity are variable, and relapses remain common."];
  "S19" [label="(19,0,0) Current therapies targeting B cells and complement have considerably improved disease management."];
  "S2" [label="(2,0,0) Broadly B cell-targeting therapies are effective, indicating B cells play a pivotal role."];
  "S20" [label="(20,0,0) Hence, it is assumed that B cells and especially autoreactive antibodies are crucially involved in disease pathogenesis."];
  "S21" [label="(21,0,0) This notion is supported by copious evidence from clinical, in vivo and in vitro studies."];
  "S22" [label="(22,0,0) Most patients require long-term, extensive immunosuppressive treatment with considerable side effects."];
  "S24" [label="(24,0,0) Therefore, it remains crucial to understand the specific pathophysiological role of B cells in both disease relapses and remission."];
  "S25" [label="(25,0,0) ANCA and, in particular, anti-MPO-ANCA are thought to be directly pathogenic."];
  "S26" [label="(26,0,0) Anti-MPO-IgG induced in mice mediated severe vasculitis when injected into wild-type mice."];
  "S27" [label="(27,0,0) The alternative pathway of the complement system was identified as a crucial mediator of anti-MPO-IgG induced pathogenicity."];
  "S28" [label="(28,0,0) In humans, the C5a receptor antagonist avacopan clearly improves disease."];
  "S29" [label="(29,0,0) Experiments deciphering in vivo pathogenicity of anti-PR3 antibodies have given varying results."];
  "S3" [label="(3,0,0) Targeting B cells can offer valuable insights into which B cell subsets contribute to disease."];
  "S30" [label="(30,0,0) Multiple in vitro experiments have demonstrated direct effects of ANCA on neutrophils."];
  "S31" [label="(31,0,0) Additionally, ANCA increase adherence of neutrophils to, and cytotoxicity towards, endothelial cells."];
  "S32" [label="(32,0,0) ANCA-stimulated neutrophils release NETs containing autoantigens and complement activating components."];
  "S33" [label="(33,0,0) It has proven challenging to study specific B cell responses underlying ANCA production in human AAV."];
  "S34" [label="(34,0,0) The biology of these cells may hold important information as to their generation and dynamics of activation."];
  "S36" [label="(36,0,0) Previous work has indicated the presence of MPO-reactive B cells in the circulation of AAV patients."];
  "S37" [label="(37,0,0) Here, we perform an analysis of the anti-IgM B cell compartment and show that most MPO-directed B cells are IgM-positive."];
  "S38" [label="(38,0,0) Analyzing the anti-MPO-Ig response, we provide the first evidence that anti-MPO-IgM may have a prominent function."];
  "S39" [label="(39,0,0) This function may relate to complement activation, as capacity is strongly dependent on anti-MPO IgM."];
  "S4" [label="(4,0,0) The mechanism by which B cells contribute to autoimmune diseases is often unknown."];
  "S40" [label="(40,0,0) Together, these results are relevant for future management of disease relapses and the design of targeted therapies."];
  "S41" [label="(41,0,0) Moreover, these results highlight IgM B cell autoreactivity as an important component of pathogenicity."];
  "S5" [label="(5,0,0) A profound mechanistic understanding is important as broadly B cell depleting interventions carry substantial risks."];
  "S9" [label="(9,0,0) A prototypic human autoimmune disease mediated by B cells is ANCA-associated vasculitis (AAV)."];
